00:48:56,842 --> 00:49:02,842
The Godfather is a trilogy of American crime films directed by Francis Ford Coppola inspired
by the 1969 novel of the same name by Italian American author Mario Puzo.

11
00:53:50,526 --> 00:53:56,526
The films follow the trials of the fictional Italian American mafia Corleone family whose
patriarch, Vito Corleone, rises to be a major figure in American organized crime.

12
00:58:44,210 --> 00:58:50,210
His youngest son, Michael Corleone, becomes his successor.

13
01:03:37,894 --> 01:03:43,894
The films were distributed by Paramount Pictures and
released in 1972, 1974, and 1990.

14
01:08:31,578 --> 01:08:37,578
The series achieved success at the box office, with the films
earning between $430 and $517 million worldwide.

15
01:13:25,263 --> 01:13:31,263
The Godfather and The Godfather Part II are both seen by
many as two of the greatest films of all time.

16
01:18:18,947 --> 01:18:24,947
The series is heavily awarded, winning 9 out of 28 Academy Award
nominations and 5 out of 20 Golden Globe Awards.

17
01:23:12,631 --> 01:23:18,631
The film explores themes of witness protection, palermo,
sicily, biography, mafia boss, family secrets.

18
01:28:06,315 --> 01:28:12,315
The tone is thought_provoking.
